.TH GETUID 2
.SH NAME
getuid, getgid, geteuid, getegid \- get user and group identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "getuid( )"
.PP
.B "geteuid( )"
.PP
.B "getgid( )"
.PP
.B "getegid( )"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getuid
returns the real user ID of the current process,
.B geteuid
the
effective user ID.
The real user ID identifies the person who is logged in,
in contradistinction to the effective user ID, which determines his access
permission at the moment.
It is thus useful to programs which operate
using the `set user ID' mode, to find out who invoked them.
.PP
.B getgid
returns the real group ID,
.B getegid
the effective group ID.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
setuid(2)
.SH ASSEMBLER
(getuid = 24.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys getuid
R0 = real UID
R1 = effective UID
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 24
int 0Xf1
AX = real UID
DX = effective UID
.fi
.PP
(getgid = 47.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = real GID
R1 = effective GID
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 47
int 0Xf1
AX = real GID
DX = effective GID
.fi
.sp
